cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference NeuroCraft Fly, cite the project landing page using the
  preferred citation below. If you use this local software candidate, also
  record its version and source revision. Cite the original MaleCNS
  reconstruction separately when using its data.
title: NeuroCraft Fly
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Evan
    website: https://github.com/evnsnclr
version: 0.2.0-rc.5
abstract: >-
  Local release candidate for an interactive Minecraft demo with modeled
  dynamics on a retained MaleCNS fruit-fly connectome. Engineered inputs and
  hand-chosen neural readouts select and modulate scripted body programs.
  Includes a separate small-fixture research tutorial. This metadata does not
  announce software publication or independent installation qualification.
repository-code: https://github.com/evnsnclr/neurocraft-fly-public
url: https://github.com/evnsnclr/neurocraft-fly-public
license: MIT
preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: NeuroCraft Fly
  authors:
    - family-names: Smith
      given-names: Evan
  year: 2026
  url: https://github.com/evnsnclr/neurocraft-fly-public
  notes: Project landing page; software release is in preparation.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - computational neuroscience
  - Minecraft
  - reproducible experiments
references:
  - type: article
    title: Sexual dimorphism in the complete Drosophila male central nervous system connectome
    authors:
      - family-names: Berg
        given-names: Stuart
      - family-names: Beckett
        given-names: Isabella R.
      - family-names: Costa
        given-names: Marta
    journal: Cell
    volume: 189
    issue: 18
    start: 5504
    end: 5526
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015
    notes: >-
      The MaleCNS v1.0 reconstruction this project derives its network from, pages
      5504-5526.e15. The article lists 111 authors; the first three are given here.
      The pinned
      acquisition manifest records the bioRxiv v2 preprint that was current at
      acquisition, doi:10.1101/2025.10.09.680999.
